  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented a set of structural changes to resolve the persistent blank screen issue.\n\n### Diagnosis & Fixes:\n- **Forced Development Mode**: I explicitly forced the backend server into `development` mode using a fixed environment variable in `server.ts`. This ensures that Vite\'s modern middleware is strictly responsible for serving your code in the preview, bypassing any stale or cached production builds.\n- **Flattened Routing Logic**: I restructured the navigation tree in `App.tsx` by removing complex nested route wrappers. This eliminates \"silent failures\" where the application might crash internally while trying to resolve its location.\n- **Enhanced CSS Stability**: I refactored the global CSS (`index.css`) to use more standard browser variables and simplified the Tailwind configuration. This prevents the styles from failing to compile and hiding the app\'s content.\n- **Fallback UI Initialization**: I added a \"Safe Initializer\" to the `index.html` file. Even before the JavaScript fully loads, you should now see a status message saying **\"Initializing KitchenPro System...\"**. If you see this message but the app still stays white, it will help us narrow down the issue to the final JavaScript execution step.\n- **Animation Isolation**: I temporarily disabled complex sidebar animations to confirm whether the animation engine was conflicting with the browser\'s rendering of the iframe.\n\n### Current Status:\nThe application is now re-compiled and the development server has been restarted with these structural safeguards. The preview should now correctly load the **KitchenPro Hub** dashboard. \n\nIf it still appears white, please check if the text \"Initializing KitchenPro System...\" is visible, as that will confirm the HTML is rendering and the issue lies strictly in the browser\'s JavaScript execution."
