    user_intent: "Theme Application & Bug Fixing\n\nThe user\'s primary goal is to ensure the \"Production & Multi-Kitchen Module\" is visually consistent with the \"Professional Polish\" design theme and to resolve any display errors that prevent the theme from rendering correctly. This involves applying theme styles to all components and fixing bugs, such as the incorrect display of white backgrounds, that hinder the intended aesthetic. The user is currently focused on troubleshooting a persistent blank screen issue in the application preview."
    session_summary: "The primary objective of this session was to apply the \"Professional Polish\" design theme to the \"Production & Multi-Kitchen Module\" and resolve rendering issues, specifically a persistent blank screen.\n\n### User\'s Main Goals:\n1.  **Theme Application**: Ensure the \"Production & Multi-Kitchen Module\" visually aligns with the \"Professional Polish\" design theme.\n2.  **Bug Fixing**: Resolve display errors, including the blank white screen issue, that prevent the theme from rendering correctly.\n\n### Key Information and Context:\n\n*   **Project Setup**: The project utilizes Vite for building and a React-based frontend. A mock Express.js server (`server.ts`) is used for API endpoints.\n*   **Design System (\"Professional Polish\")**:\n    *   **Color Palette**: Primary (#4F46E5), Background (#F8FAFC), Text (#1E293B), Muted Text (#64748B), Success (#22C55E), Warning (#F59E0B), Border (#E2E8F0).\n    *   **Corner Radius**: `rounded-2xl` (16px) for cards, `rounded-lg` (8px) for buttons/inputs.\n    *   **Shadows**: `shadow-sm` for default, `shadow-md` for hover states.\n    *   **Typography**: Inter font family.\n    *   **Animations**: Framer Motion (`motion`) was intended for page transitions and modal entries.\n*   **Module Structure**: The application is divided into Admin and Chef sections, with various pages like Dashboard, Planning, Kitchen Detail, Wastage Reports, Chef Queue, and Chef Stock.\n*   **Core Components**: `Shell` (Layout), `Card`, `Button`, `Badge`, `Modal`.\n*   **Key Libraries**:\n    *   `react`, `react-dom`, `react-router-dom`\n    *   `tailwindcss`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `autoprefixer`\n    *   `lucide-react` (icons)\n    *   `recharts` (charts)\n    *   `motion` (from `motion/react` for animations)\n    *   `clsx`, `tailwind-merge` (for class name utility)\n    *   `vite`\n    *   `express`, `@types/express`\n    *   `tsx` (for running TS server)\n*   **Dependencies & APIs**:\n    *   `@google/genai` (though not actively used in the provided code, it\'s listed)\n    *   Mock API service defined in `services/api.ts`.\n    *   Types defined in `types.ts`.\n\n### Existing Blockers and Bugs:\n\n1.  **Persistent Blank White Screen**: This was the most critical issue. Despite multiple attempts to apply styles and fix imports, the application preview remained blank.\n2.  **Path Alias Resolution Errors**: The `@/` path alias in `vite.config.ts` was causing runtime errors because `__dirname` is not reliably available in ESM environments, leading to import failures.\n3.  **CSS Compilation Issues**: An invalid Tailwind utility class (`lowercase-none`) was previously identified and removed, which had caused a build crash.\n4.  **Animation Conflicts**: The use of `motion` from `motion/react` and potentially complex animations in `Shell.tsx` and `Card.tsx` were suspected as potential sources of rendering conflicts, especially in the preview environment.\n5.  **Missing Global Styles**: The Inter font was not correctly loaded globally, and some CSS variables were not being applied as expected.\n\n### Actions Taken:\n\n*   **Import Refactoring**: All path aliases (`@/src/...`) were systematically replaced with relative paths (e.g., `../../lib/utils`). `vite.config.ts` was updated to remove the problematic alias.\n*   **CSS Stabilization**:\n    *   Global CSS (`index.css`) was refactored to use standard CSS variables and ensure proper font loading.\n    *   Hardcoded `slate-` styles were removed from components to enforce theme consistency.\n*   **Loading States Implementation**: Visual loading indicators (spinners with text) were added to `Dashboard.tsx` and `KitchenDetail.tsx` to provide feedback during data fetching, replacing blank `null` returns.\n*   **Routing Simplification**: Nested routes in `App.tsx` were flattened, and fallback routes were improved for better stability.\n*   **Server Environment Control**: The `server.ts` was modified to explicitly set `process.env.NODE_ENV` to `\'development\'` to ensure Vite\'s middleware mode functions correctly.\n*   **Animation Isolation**: Animations in `Shell.tsx` and `Card.tsx` were temporarily disabled to rule them out as the cause of the blank screen.\n*   **HTML Title Update**: The `index.html` title was updated to \"KitchenPro Hub\", and an initial \"Initializing KitchenPro System...\" message was added to the `#root` div for better debugging.\n*   **Final Compiles and Restarts**: Multiple `compile_applet` and `restart_dev_server` actions were performed to ensure changes were applied and the environment was reset.\n\n### Next Steps:\n\n1.  **Re-enable Animations Incrementally**: Once the application is confirmed to be rendering correctly without the blank screen, reintroduce animations from `motion/react` step-by-step, starting with simpler components like `Modal.tsx` and `Card.tsx`, and then `Shell.tsx`. Test thoroughly after each re-introduction.\n2.  **Verify Full Theme Application**: Conduct a final visual inspection of all pages and components to ensure every element adheres to the \"Professional Polish\" design specifications (colors, spacing, typography, borders, shadows).\n3.  **Test Role-Based Routing**: Confirm that switching between \'Admin\' and \'Chef\' roles correctly navigates the user to their respective sections and that all routes are accessible and functional.\n4.  **API Integration Check**: Ensure all data fetching and display (e.g., Dashboard stats, Activity Feed, Kitchen Details) are working as expected with the mock API.\n5.  **Code Linting and Formatting**: Run a final `lint` command to catch any remaining code style or type issues."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>16-47;26-47</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Simplified the routing structure in App.tsx by removing nested Route wrappers and flattening the navigation tree to resolve potential rendering conflicts and improve routing reliability.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/index.css</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>1-21;1-34</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Refactored global CSS in index.css to use standard browser variables and simplified Tailwind configuration, ensuring correct UI rendering and preventing compilation issues.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/components/layout/Shell.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>34-34</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Temporarily disabled sidebar animations in Shell.tsx to isolate and diagnose potential conflicts with the animation engine that might be causing the blank screen issue.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/pages/admin/Dashboard.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>29-29</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Replaced the null return with a visual loading spinner and status message in Dashboard.tsx, improving the user experience by providing feedback during data fetching.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/pages/admin/KitchenDetail.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>26-26</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Implemented a loading indicator in KitchenDetail.tsx to manage user expectations during data retrieval and prevent a blank screen.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/main.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>6-6</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Standardized the App import in main.tsx to \'./App\' to align with common Vite project structures and prevent potential path resolution issues.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/vite.config.ts</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>15-15</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Removed the path alias configuration from vite.config.ts to eliminate potential runtime conflicts and simplify module resolution after converting all imports to relative paths.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/server.ts</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>6-6</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Forced the server into development mode by setting process.env.NODE_ENV to \'development\' in server.ts, ensuring Vite\'s middleware handles code serving correctly in the preview environment.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/index.html</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>5-10</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Updated the HTML title to \"KitchenPro Hub\" and added an initialization message to index.html to provide a visible fallback during the debugging phase.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>26-47</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Restored the full application routing and state management logic in App.tsx after successfully resolving path resolution and server connectivity issues.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>26-47</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Simplified the navigation tree in App.tsx by removing nested Route wrappers to resolve potential blank screen issues caused by complex route nesting.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/components/ui/Card.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>15-24</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Removed motion animations from the Card component to isolate and diagnose if framer-motion is causing the blank screen issue.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/metadata.json</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-7</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>The metadata.json file contains the application\'s name and description. It was reviewed to ensure it accurately reflected the \"Production & Multi-Kitchen Module\" and to check for any inconsistencies that might indirectly affect rendering.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/package.json</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-41</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>The package.json file was reviewed to check the versions of installed animation libraries (framer-motion/motion) and UI components. This was important for ensuring compatibility and identifying potential conflicts that could lead to runtime errors.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/src/components/ui/Card.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-29</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>The Card component was viewed to assess its use of motion animations. This was done in preparation for removing these animations to help isolate the cause of the blank screen issue.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx: AppContent component</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The AppContent component\'s routing logic was simplified by removing nested Route wrappers and flattening the structure. This was a key step in resolving potential rendering conflicts and improving routing reliability, which was suspected to be a cause of the blank screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>index.css: Global Styles</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The global CSS was refactored to use standard browser variables and a simplified Tailwind configuration. This was crucial for ensuring correct UI rendering and preventing compilation issues that could lead to a blank screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>server.ts: process.env.NODE_ENV assignment</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The server was explicitly forced into development mode by setting `process.env.NODE_ENV` to \'development\'. This ensures that Vite\'s modern middleware is used for code serving in the preview, bypassing potential issues with stale production builds.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>index.html: Initializing KitchenPro System...</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>An initialization message was added to index.html. This provides a visible fallback, confirming that the HTML is rendering and helping to pinpoint whether the blank screen issue originates from JavaScript execution.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>src/components/layout/Shell.tsx: Sidebar animation logic</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>Motion animations within the sidebar component were temporarily disabled. This was done to diagnose if the animation engine was conflicting with the browser\'s rendering in the iframe, potentially causing the blank screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>"
