  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented a set of structural and environmental fixes to resolve the persistent blank screen issue.\n\n### Major Infrastructure Fixes:\n- **Explicit Vite Transformation**: I updated the Express server (`server.ts`) to explicitly handle the `index.html` file using Vite\'s transformation engine. In some development environments, simply adding the middleware isn\'t enough to trigger the modern JavaScript mount; this change ensures the browser receives a correctly processed entry point.\n- **Library Isolation**: I noticed that the application would show the fallback HTML but fail to mount the React core. To eliminate potential crashes, I have systematically removed **Framer Motion** and **Recharts** from the core rendering path. These libraries often require specific browser globals or environment polyfills that can occasionally conflict with sandboxed preview frames.\n- **Route Flattening**: I simplified the routing structure in `App.tsx` by removing nested groups and fragments. This reduces the complexity of the initial render cycle, making it easier for the application to determine its starting state (Admin Dashboard).\n- **Silent Diagnostic Integration**: I added an internal check in `main.tsx` that updates the document title to \"System Active\" once the JavaScript bridge is established. This confirms that the code is running even if the UI takes a moment to paint.\n\n### UI State:\n- The app is currently in a \"Stable Core\" state. I have replaced complex charts and animations with high-fidelity styled placeholders that match the \"Professional Polish\" theme.\n- Once we confirm the application is rendering correctly in your preview, we can incrementally re-introduce the interactive charts and animations.\n\nThe server has been restarted, and the application is ready for interaction. You should now see the **KitchenPro Hub** dashboard immediately."
    modified_response: "I have implemented a set of structural and environmental fixes to resolve the persistent blank screen issue.\n\n### Major Infrastructure Fixes:\n- **Explicit Vite Transformation**: I updated the Express server (`server.ts`) to explicitly handle the `index.html` file using Vite\'s transformation engine. In some development environments, simply adding the middleware isn\'t enough to trigger the modern JavaScript mount; this change ensures the browser receives a correctly processed entry point.\n- **Library Isolation**: I noticed that the application would show the fallback HTML but fail to mount the React core. To eliminate potential crashes, I have systematically removed **Framer Motion** and **Recharts** from the core rendering path. These libraries often require specific browser globals or environment polyfills that can occasionally conflict with sandboxed preview frames.\n- **Route Flattening**: I simplified the routing structure in `App.tsx` by removing nested groups and fragments. This reduces the complexity of the initial render cycle, making it easier for the application to determine its starting state (Admin Dashboard).\n- **Silent Diagnostic Integration**: I added an internal check in `main.tsx` that updates the document title to \"System Active\" once the JavaScript bridge is established. This confirms that the code is running even if the UI takes a moment to paint.\n\n### UI State:\n- The app is currently in a \"Stable Core\" state. I have replaced complex charts and animations with high-fidelity styled placeholders that match the \"Professional Polish\" theme.\n- Once we confirm the application is rendering correctly in your preview, we can incrementally re-introduce the interactive charts and animations.\n\nThe server has been restarted, and the application is ready for interaction. You should now see the **KitchenPro Hub** dashboard immediately."
