t modern JavaScript features and module transformations are correctly applied, which is crucial for the SPA to mount properly.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx: Minimal static content</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The entire React application structure was replaced with a very basic static HTML display. This is a debugging step to confirm if React can render *anything* in the current environment, isolating the problem from routing, state management, or complex component logic.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>main.tsx: Console log and document title update</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>Adding `console.log(\'Mounting App...\')` and `document.title = \\\"System Active\\\";` provides immediate feedback in the browser\'s developer console and tab title, confirming that the JavaScript is executing and the React app is attempting to mount.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>src/index.css: Minimal baseline styles</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The global CSS was reduced to the bare minimum to eliminate any possibility of CSS parsing errors or conflicts causing the white screen issue. This ensures that only Tailwind\'s base styles and essential body resets are applied.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>components/ui/Card.tsx, components/ui/Badge.tsx, components/ui/Modal.tsx, pages/admin/KitchenDetail.tsx: Removal of Framer Motion</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>Framer Motion was systematically removed from all UI components and pages. This is a critical step in debugging, as animation libraries can sometimes cause rendering conflicts or require specific environment setups that might not be present in the preview.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>pages/admin/Dashboard.tsx, pages/admin/WastageReport.tsx: Removal of Recharts</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>Recharts was r